Chrome Glass Remastered - acknowledgement
=========================================

Chrome Glass Remastered is an unofficial, derivative remaster of:

    "Chrome Glass" by RPGFX
    Published on WinCustomize (CursorFX), 13 April 2006
    https://www.wincustomize.com/explore/cursorfx/1875

Ten days later the same set appeared on DeviantArt under the name of yoyos
(23 April 2006, https://www.deviantart.com/yoyos/art/Chrome-Glass-32252748),
someone else's work passed off as their own. Earlier releases of this
remaster took that copy for the original. The design is by RPGFX.

The frames in art/orig/ are the original 2006 bitmaps, extracted from the
.ani files of the DeviantArt copy. The frames in art/ai/ are AI upscales of
them, used only to trace the outlines in data/traced.json; nothing the
network drew reaches a cursor. The shipped cursors (dist/, release archives,
previews) are drawn anew on those outlines, after the original artist's
work. The Pin and Person cursors are new drawings made for this set in the
original's style.

The "Chrome Glass" name and the original artwork remain the creative work
and property of their author; "HD" marks this as an unofficial remaster.
It is published as a tribute, in the belief that a free,
attribution-preserving revival of a 20-year-old classic is in its spirit.
If you are the author and want anything changed or removed, open an issue
and it will be done.

If you build on this project, keep this acknowledgement. Before any use
beyond this repository (forks aside), consider contacting the original
author on WinCustomize.

The MIT license in LICENSE covers the code only (build pipeline, tracing,
rendering and packaging tools), not the cursor artwork.
